 {
  "kind": 1,
  "language": "markdown",
  "value": "# Setup: Variables and the Heat Limit\n\n**Goal:** Configure your weather station's location, email settings, and default heat threshold before starting the labs.\n\n> **Nothing to run in this notebook:** The lines below are **broker commands** and a **published MQTT message** — not LoT code cells.\n\n**Where things are in the Coreflux HUB:**\n- **Bottom dock:** Opens **Data Viewer**, **Connectors**, **LoT Editor**, and **Dashboards** (hover over any icon to see its name).\n- **Top-right user menu (`root`):** Opens **Command Console**, **Broker Settings**, and **Log out**. Your active licence tier (*Community*, or your event licence) is shown right next to it."
 },
 {
  "kind": 1,
  "language": "markdown",
  "value": "## Step 1: Set Your Variables and Secret\n\nIn the HUB, click **`root`** at the top right, open **Command Console**, and send these commands one at a time:\n\n```\n-setEnv WEATHER_LAT=40.7128\n-setEnv WEATHER_LON=-74.0060\n-setEnv SMTP_HOST=mailpit\n-setEnv SMTP_USER=weather@example.com\n-setSecret SMTP_PASSWORD=any-password\n```\n\nEach command replies with a line of JSON containing `\"success\":true` and *… set successfully*.\n\n- **`WEATHER_LAT` / `WEATHER_LON`** are your station's latitude and longitude (the example coordinates are New York — feel free to use your own city!).\n- Write `NAME=value` with **no spaces** around `=`.\n- **Tip:** You can also add or inspect these visually in **Broker Settings → Variables & Secrets**."
 },
 {
  "kind": 1,
  "language": "markdown",
  "value": "## Step 2: Publish the Initial Heat Limit\n\nOpen **Data Viewer** from the bottom dock, click **Publish** (the paper-plane icon on the left), and publish:\n\n- **Topic:** `config/heat_limit_c`\n- **Payload:** `30`\n- **Retain:** Switched **ON**\n\nThis sets the heat-alert threshold in °C. Because **Retain** is on, the Broker remembers `30` on `config/heat_limit_c` so `HeatAlert` (in Lab 4) can read it at any time."
 },
 {
  "kind": 1,
  "language": "markdown",
  "value": "## Check It Worked\n\n- **Broker Settings → Variables & Secrets:** You should see the four variables under **Variables**, and `SMTP_PASSWORD` under **Secrets** (secret values are encrypted and never shown).\n- **Data Viewer:** In the topic tree on the left, expand `config` → `heat_limit_c` and confirm its value is `30`.\n\n**Next:** Open `01-heartbeat.lotnb`."
 }
]
